kylin-nm (4.20.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Port project to Qt6 and KF6:
    - debian/control: Update Build-Depends from qtbase5-dev/libkf5* to
      qt6-base-dev and libkf6* packages.
    - debian/rules: Update build system to use qmake6 instead of qt5-qmake.
  * Update Build-Depends in debian/control:
    - Add Kylin SDK and UKUI dependencies: libkysdk-applications-dev, 
      libkysdk-system-dev, libukcc-dev, libukui-common-dev, 
      libukui-log4qt-dev, libukui-quick-dev.
    - Add NetworkManager libs: libnm-dev, libnma-dev,
      libkf6networkmanagerqt-dev.
    - Add other deps: libcap-dev, libgtk-3-dev, libsecret-1-dev,
      dh-sequence-systemd.
    - Remove obsolete deps: libqt5x11extras5-dev, qtscript5-dev.
  * Update Runtime Depends in debian/control:
    - Add specific network-manager plugins (gnome, l2tp, openvpn, pptp,
      strongswan).
    - Add ukui-control-center and libkysdk runtime dependencies.
  * Update debian/rules:
    - Add override_dh_installsystemd to explicitly enable and start 
      kylin-nm-sysdbus service.
    - Add override_dh_shlibdeps to ignore missing info.
  * Add maintainer scripts:
    - Add debian/kylin-nm.postinst and debian/kylin-nm.preinst.

 -- zhangpan <zhangpan@kylinos.cn>  Wed, 28 Jan 2026 15:01:51 +0800

